{
 "node": "LayerSet",
 "mode": "scene",
 "note": "the world draws a red box at the origin, layer 1 a blue box behind it (z -5), layer 2 a green box off to the right. Probed from the composited frame in both engines: with order 0 1 the blue box shows in front of the red one (depth is cleared between layers), with order 1 0 the red one is in front, with order 0 only the world shows, with 0 1 2 the green box appears; visible FALSE takes a layer out. The body's neutral tone map shifts pure colours, so the tolerance is 45.; hovering: the top drawn layer that has a hit wins, a layer with pointerEvents FALSE or one that is not drawn is passed over (both engines)",
 "gaps": [
  "activeLayer (which layer the user navigates) and the navigation of a layer's own Viewpoint are held, not acted on: the user always navigates the world's camera",
  "a layer's Viewpoint is read once and per frame, not bound or animated; the layer has no NavigationInfo, Background or headlight of its own",
  "lights of the world light the meshes of every layer; a layer has no lights of its own",
  "order without any visible layer draws the world (Babylon needs a camera)"
